d's holdings-disclosure policy, including frequency, timing and who receives the information.\n- **Daily public holdings:** Standard UCITS ETFs publish their full portfolio daily, alongside an indicative NAV (iNAV), so market makers can price and hedge.\n- **Conditional periodic-holdings route:** A fund (typically actively managed or semi-transparent) may disclose holdings less often than daily. In that case it generally must give authorised participants and market makers alternative daily information, such as a basket or proxy portfolio and an iNAV, so that arbitrage still works. The exact conditions should be checked against the cited guidance.","ttft_ms":4137,"type":"result","duration_ms":5315,"uuid":"73dad756-fa56-496d-b9e4-5431587f2409","ttft_stream_ms":444,"time_to_request_ms":72,"first_content_frame_ms":444,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
